# Level and Pulled-Back Entrance Camera

Status: DONE
Milestone: M44 A straight default view with room for the shop interior
Dependencies: 39_ARCHITECTURAL_BAKERY_FACADE.todo; 42_PHONE_TILT_ENTRANCE.todo

## Purpose

The owner says the default entrance camera looks down too much and asks for a
straight view, with the camera pulled back or the building scaled to fit.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve the existing camera and three fallback posters.
- [x] Level the default optical axis and pull the camera back without stretching the facade.
- [x] Compensate bounded look-around travel for the greater viewing distance.
- [x] Regenerate matching wide/portrait/short fallback views from the same lit room.
- [x] Check neutral horizon, cake/footing visibility and mouse/phone look-around.
- [x] Complete full site/fallback checks, refresh the entrance artwork/docs and publish.

## Acceptance criteria

- Neutral eye and target are at the same height; no default downward pitch.
- Camera is farther back and the display occupies less of the glazing.
- Scene geometry, fixed lighting, baked illumination and facade dimensions remain unchanged.
- All four cake landmarks remain visible; counter support and strong look-around remain.
- Static posters match the live camera; local4174experiment is untouched.

